{"format":1,"key":"zone:azshara","path":"/lore/zone/azshara","name":"Azshara","kind":"zone","label":"Zone","zone":{"key":"azshara","name":"Azshara","path":"/lore/zone/azshara"},"levels":"","description":"Azshara is a rugged, windswept coastline in northeastern Kalimdor cloaked in vibrant, perpetual autumn foliage. Once part of the glorious night elven…","intro":[],"clips":[{"id":"zone:azshara","part":"narration","anchor":"story","title":"The story","paras":["Azshara is a rugged, windswept coastline in northeastern Kalimdor cloaked in vibrant, perpetual autumn foliage. Once part of the glorious night elven capital before the Great Sundering shattered it into the sea, it remains a dangerous wilderness littered with ancient ruins, brooding naga, and isolated practitioners of magic. Both the Horde and the Alliance maintain precarious outposts along its borders, wary of the restless ghosts and ocean horrors lurking within.","Ten thousand years ago, this coast was the beating heart of the kaldorei civilization, surrounding the royal capital of Zin-Azshari. When Queen Azshara and her Highborne court drew the Burning Legion into Azeroth, the resulting War of the Ancients culminated in the catastrophic collapse of the Well of Eternity. The sea thundered inward, swallowing most of the magnificent city and leaving behind fractured cliffs, treacherous coral reefs, and waterlogged spires. The survivors renamed the ruined landscape after their fallen monarch, branding it as a cursed monument to pride and catastrophic betrayal.","Azshara is famous for its stunning crimson, orange, and gold canopy, giving the impression of an eternal autumn unbroken by changing seasons. Beneath this tranquil canopy, however, lies an inhospitable expanse. Corrupted satyrs practice dark rituals in forested hollows, lingering Highborne apparitions haunt drowned foundations, and Spitelash naga prowl the shallow reefs of the Coral Sea. Ferocious beasts, giant hydras, and mountain giants roam unchecked across the highlands and ivory beaches.","Because of its isolation and harsh terrain, Azshara draws recluse figures pursuing forgotten crafts or watching over dangerous powers. The enigmatic Archmage Xylem inhabits a secluded tower perched high above the cliffs, testing promising spellcasters and cunning rogues alike. Farther along the coast, the demon hunter Loramus Thalipedes watches the waves from a barren isle, while the immense sea giant Lord Arkkoroc demands blood sacrifices from his temple overlooking the churning waters."],"hash":"083fb6","voices":{"male-narrator":{"sha":"9b97ccb731","sec":125},"female-narrator":{"sha":"ab5e1a1b35","sec":131}}}],"sources":[{"kind":"wiki","title":"Azshara (Classic)","url":"https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Azshara_(Classic)"},{"kind":"wiki","title":"Azshara","url":"https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Azshara"}],"related":[{"p":"/lore/zone/ashenvale","n":"Ashenvale","k":"zone"},{"p":"/lore/zone/durotar","n":"Durotar","k":"zone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/ruins-of-eldarath","n":"Ruins of Eldarath","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/bay-of-storms","n":"Bay of Storms","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/temple-of-arkkoran","n":"Temple of Arkkoran","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/lake-mennar","n":"Lake Mennar","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/zone/winterspring","n":"Winterspring","k":"zone"},{"p":"/lore/npc/andron-gant","n":"Andron Gant","k":"npc"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/bladefist-bay","n":"Bladefist Bay","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/npc/asterion","n":"Asterion","k":"npc"},{"p":"/lore/quest/6543-the-warsong-reports","n":"The Warsong Reports","k":"quest"},{"p":"/lore/item/warsong-outrider-update","n":"Warsong Outrider Update","k":"item"}],"children":[{"p":"/lore/subzone/bay-of-storms","n":"Bay of Storms","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/bear-s-head","n":"Bear's Head","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/bitter-reaches","n":"Bitter Reaches","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/forlorn-ridge","n":"Forlorn Ridge","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/haldarr-encamp